From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SnowballMC <noreply@snowballmc.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Offload bounded flat ground path recomputations

Motivated by Leaf 0092, Petal: Async Pathfinding (peaches94, fixed/updated
by KaiijuMC; Petal and Kaiiju upstreams, GPL-3.0-only). This is a separate
implementation: no upstream async Path, shared evaluator, or live region
is sent to workers. The detached search mirrors the bounded subset of
Minecraft's PathFinder, BinaryHeap, and WalkNodeEvaluator used here.

Path creation and explicit recomputation remain synchronous, including
plugin-visible paths. Only the internal block-update recomputation hook
can queue work. Delay navigation for at most two ticks; replace on the
server thread only after revalidating the complete capture and intent.

